message.content:
These are MDF cabinet doors and drawer fronts, which are parts of furniture. Wooden furniture parts fall under 9403.91 ("Parts of wooden furniture"). The relevant subheading is 9403.91.00, with statistical suffix 9403.91.0080 for "Other" parts of wooden furniture. I recall CBP rulings on cabinet doors of MDF classifying them in 9403.91.0080.

The alternative is 4418 (builders' joinery), but cabinet doors for furniture are furniture parts, not building joinery. Chapter 94 covers furniture parts under note 1(g), so 9403.91 fits.

{"hts_code": "9403.91.0080", "reason": "Pre-finished MDF cabinet door and drawer components are identifiable parts of wooden furniture (kitchen, vanity, wardrobe cabinets), classified in heading 9403 as parts of wooden furniture, subheading 9403.91."}
